{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":58974,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"84584b94-61ab-5e70-8a05-74a2b96f8e7c","total_cost_usd":0.438322,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8418,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":5305,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8418,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5305,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8418,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8418},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4612,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.004692,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":5305,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":8418,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.43363,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\": \"actor:dependence-free-batch-a-reviewer-fable-16\", \"reviews\": [{\"case_id\": \"case:6da5419523f5f9dbedf9\", \"verdict\": \"demonstrated_issue\", \"issue_class\": \"issue-class:repeated-authorized-independent-unit-entry-into-row-independent-procedure\", \"bounded_statement\": \"Within the supplied files, the report's selected result (two-sample Student t-test, t(46) = -7.67, p < 0.001, Cohen's d = -2.21) was computed by entering all 48 rise readings as separate observations, even though the data description designates jar_id as the independent unit and each of the 12 jars contributes 4 repeated readings from the same batch of dough. The 46 degrees of freedom confirm that 48 rows, not 12 jars, were treated as independent units, so the reported precision (p-value, df, effect size) overstates the evidence available from 12 independent jars. This finding is bounded to the statistical validity of the selected result; the direction of the rye-versus-spelt difference is consistent at the jar level and is not itself contested.\", \"root_cause\": \"The workflow pools rise_mm values by flour_type only (rise_by_flour groups on flour_type and discards jar_id for analysis purposes) and passes all per-reading values directly into scipy.stats.ttest_ind, a procedure that assumes each row is an independent observation. No aggregation to jar-level summaries (e.g., per-jar means) and no repeated-measures/mixed model was used, so the four correlated readings per jar were counted as four independent observations each, inflating the effective sample size from 12 jars to 48 rows and hence inflating df (46 instead of 10), deflating the p-value, and distorting Cohen's d.\", \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The data description explicitly names jar_id as the independent-unit column and states one row is a single timed measurement from a jar, so rows within a jar are repeated measures, not independent units.\", \"observed_value\": \"Independent unit column: jar_id; one row = one timed measurement from a single jar\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"data-description.md\", \"start_line\": 21, \"end_line\": 22, \"quoted_text\": \"One row is: one timed measurement of rise height and pH taken from a single starter jar at a single incubation time\\nIndependent unit column: jar_id\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The description states each jar appears four times in the file and that those four numbers come from the same batch of dough, establishing within-jar dependence of rows.\", \"observed_value\": \"4 rows per jar, same batch of dough\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"data-description.md\", \"start_line\": 9, \"end_line\": 10, \"quoted_text\": \"Because of that schedule, each jar shows up in the file four times, once per\\nvisit, and those four numbers come from the same batch of dough.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The description states treatment (flour) is assigned at the jar level, not the measurement level, so the jar is the experimental unit for the flour comparison.\", \"observed_value\": \"flour treatment belongs to the jar\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"data-description.md\", \"start_line\": 5, \"end_line\": 6, \"quoted_text\": \"cabinet: six jars were fed rye flour and six were fed spelt flour, so the flour\\ntreatment belongs to the jar, not to any single measurement.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The workflow groups rise_mm by flour_type only, discarding jar identity, so all per-reading values from the same jar enter the analysis vector as separate elements.\", \"observed_value\": \"grouping key is flour_type; jar_id not used in the test\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 19, \"end_line\": 23, \"quoted_text\": \"def rise_by_flour(rows):\\n    grouped = {}\\n    for row in rows:\\n        grouped.setdefault(row[\\\"flour_type\\\"], []).append(float(row[\\\"rise_mm\\\"]))\\n    return {flour: np.array(vals, dtype=float) for flour, vals in sorted(grouped.items())}\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The workflow feeds the full per-reading vectors (24 rows per group) into a row-independent two-sample t-test and computes df from row counts (48 - 2 = 46), not jar counts (12 - 2 = 10).\", \"observed_value\": \"stats.ttest_ind on 24-vs-24 readings; dof = n_a + n_b - 2 = 46\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 45, \"end_line\": 46, \"quoted_text\": \"tstat, pvalue = stats.ttest_ind(rise_a, rise_b, equal_var=True)\\n    dof = n_a + n_b - 2\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The report explicitly states that every one of the 48 rows was entered as a separate observation into the two-sample t-test.\", \"observed_value\": \"48 rows entered as separate observations\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 15, \"end_line\": 17, \"quoted_text\": \"Every one of the 48 rows was entered as a separate observation in a two-sided,\\nequal-variance two-sample Student t-test comparing rise height between the two\\nflour types (rye minus spelt). The group summaries above use the same 48 rows.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The selected result reports t(46) and inference at the level of individual readings, confirming 48 correlated rows were treated as independent units in the reported conclusion.\", \"observed_value\": \"t(46) = -7.67, p < 0.001, Cohen's d = -2.21 over 48 readings\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 21, \"end_line\": 21, \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] Two-sample t-test over 48 rise readings: rye minus spelt = -7.00 mm, t(46) = -7.67, p < 0.001, Cohen's d = -2.21.\"}, {\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 23, \"end_line\": 24, \"quoted_text\": \"Rye jars measured about 7 mm lower than spelt jars across the 24-hour window,\\nand at the level of individual readings the gap is flagged as highly significant.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The input data confirm the repeated-row structure: e.g., jar RYE-1 appears in four consecutive rows at hours 6, 12, 18, 24, and all such rows carry the jar's single flour assignment.\", \"observed_value\": \"4 rows for jar RYE-1\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"data/input.csv\", \"start_line\": 2, \"end_line\": 5, \"quoted_text\": \"r01,RYE-1,rye,6,4.41,15\\nr02,RYE-1,rye,12,4.19,16\\nr03,RYE-1,rye,18,4.02,18\\nr04,RYE-1,rye,24,3.93,19\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The report transparently discloses the clustered design (12 jars, 4 readings each), so the repeated-entry structure is not concealed; however, disclosure does not change the fact that the statistical procedure itself treats the 48 rows as independent.\", \"observed_value\": \"12 jars, 4 readings per jar disclosed in the report\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 5, \"end_line\": 6, \"quoted_text\": \"`data/input.csv` holds 48 timed rise readings from 12 fermentation jars.\\nEach jar contributed 4 readings, taken at hours 6, 12, 18, 24 after feeding.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The direction and rough magnitude of the effect are robust: every spelt jar's readings exceed the corresponding rye jars' readings at comparable hours (e.g., all spelt readings at hour 24 are 25-32 mm versus 19-25 mm for rye), so a correct jar-level analysis would likely still find spelt rising higher; this limits the harm to inflated precision (df, p, d) rather than a wrong sign, but does not make the reported t(46) inference valid.\", \"observed_value\": \"jar-level means: rye 17.00-22.75 mm; spelt 23.50-29.50 mm (computed from data/input.csv)\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"data/input.csv\", \"start_line\": 22, \"end_line\": 26, \"quoted_text\": \"r21,RYE-6,rye,6,4.28,20\\nr22,RYE-6,rye,12,4.05,22\\nr23,RYE-6,rye,18,3.91,24\\nr24,RYE-6,rye,24,3.82,25\\nr25,SPL-1,spelt,6,4.26,22\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I tried to falsify the finding in three ways. (1) I checked whether the workflow aggregates readings to one value per jar before testing (e.g., per-jar means), which would make the row-independent t-test appropriate; it does not — jars_of() counts jars only for the descriptive table, while the test operates on rise_by_flour's per-reading vectors. (2) I checked whether the reported degrees of freedom could correspond to a jar-level analysis: a jar-level test would give t(10), but the report states t(46), matching 48 rows entered individually, and the report's own Analysis section states outright that all 48 rows were entered as separate observations. (3) I checked whether the data description might designate the reading, not the jar, as the independent unit; it explicitly names jar_id as the independent-unit column and states the four readings per jar come from the same batch of dough. All three checks confirm rather than refute the issue.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}]}","ttft_ms":24581,"ttft_stream_ms":2421,"time_to_request_ms":15,"type":"result","duration_ms":59765,"uuid":"d0e296d1-659b-4738-b0cd-bd9d72b7a7ba"}
